{"title":"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of four numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that each of the four numbers is now increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. These four new numbers are added together and then the sum is tripled. What is the value of this final result?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a4d8aa1ebebdad9cc35f586a52ed06f9491852.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 3T + 3 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 3T + 4 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 3T + 12 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ T + 12 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 12T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"597\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers and each is increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the sum would increase by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69285c6727e2935af0e074481c620dcf5345a891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 1 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, so the new sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/2/f4277caaaeea605810e2cce044f324248bfa7bb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Since this new sum is tripled, the result is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1e4e7d1476ad3e9eb051838dc427330953921d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(T + 4) = 3 \\times T + 3 \\times 4 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 3T + 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"334\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"20